Present Manim slides natively

Purpose: lecture with Manim slides inside Rnote: import the slides of a
deck, write on them, and step through their animations on the
projector. Slides come from a Manim fork whose vector backend writes
each slide as a .slide.json timeline (spec: slide-format.md in that
fork, reference evaluator SlideTimeline.evaluate). No browser engine:
the timeline is a pure function of time t.

Behaviour:
- Main menu "Import Manim Slides": multi-select .slide.json files, one
  slide per page from the page in view, on the document layer, so ink
  goes on top.
- Space/PageDown forward, Shift+Space/PageUp back, also from the
  presentation window; buttons in the presentation controls. Forward
  plays, finishes while playing, and at the end centers the next page
  and plays its slide. A slide reached by scrolling waits at its start.
  Back rewinds, then shows the previous page at its end. The typewriter
  keeps Space for typing.
- The audience always sees slides animate, unplayed ones at their
  start. The lecturer's screen shows the end state, like presenter
  notes, unless Settings > General "Animate Slides on This Screen".
- "Update Manim Slides": re-rendered files replace slides of the same
  section name in place, ink kept, one undo step.

Approach:
- crates/rnote-engine/src/manimslide/: format (unpack), timeline
  (evaluate), ops (arc, partial), draw (paint), render (piet). Tests
  compare against fixtures and PNGs of the Python reference
  (tests/data/manimslide; RNOTE_MANIM_FIXTURES checks whole decks).
- Storage: VectorImage.manim_slide (optional) holds the slide file
  verbatim (Arc<str>), its time and source file; svg_data is the end
  frame, so readers without slide support still show it.
- Playback state lives in SlidePlayer beside the store, not in the
  strokes. The store draw loops of all views ask it through the
  LiveStrokes trait and draw live slides at their stacking place.

Constraints: builds on dual-screen and projector-tablet (presentation
window, raster cache). Developed further on branch exp-manim-slides.
File format: additive optional field only.

